+
+## JSON Merge Patch
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a JSON Merge Patch ([RFC 7386](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)) to a
+target JSON document and returns the merged document. An object patch is merged member by member, recursively; a member
+whose value is `null` removes the target member of that name. A patch that is not an object, arrays included, replaces the
+whole target, and arrays in the patch replace the target value as a whole. The target and the patch are not modified.
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from './src/index.ts';
+
+applyMergePatch({ title: 'Hello', author: { name: 'Ann' }, tags: ['a'] }, {
+  title: 'Goodbye',
+  author: { name: null, email: 'ann@example.com' },
+  tags: null,
+}); // { title: 'Goodbye', author: { email: 'ann@example.com' } }
+```
+
+It throws a `SyntaxError` when the patch contains a value that is not a JSON value (`undefined`, `NaN`, a `Date`, a function...).
